---
// Beta terms of service — example-org/operations#8.
//
// Two clauses here exist because their absence elsewhere caused real harm,
// and both are written to be read rather than skipped:
//
//   Permanent data loss. A zero-knowledge service has a legal consequence
//   most competitors' terms simply do not state (Notesnook's, for one): if
//   the user loses both secrets, the data is gone, and no support ticket
//   changes that. Leaving it out would let someone sign up believing a reset
//   exists.
//
//   The end-of-beta guarantee. Skiff shut down and its users discovered the
//   terms had promised them nothing. So this says the opposite explicitly:
//   accounts continue, a paid tier would be optional, and a shutdown carries
//   90 days' notice with export working throughout (period confirmed
//   2026-08-12).
//
// The moderation paragraph is doing double duty — it is also the DSA Art. 14
// transparency requirement, which is why it describes a capability rather
// than a policy: we cannot screen content, so the terms cannot pretend we
// choose not to.
//
// German version: `nutzungsbedingungen.astro`. Same document.
import LandingLayout from "../layouts/LandingLayout.astro";
import GlassNav from "../components/GlassNav.astro";
import { absoluteOg } from "../lib/og";

const title = "Beta Terms — Myne";
const description =
  "Terms for the free Myne beta: no payment, no warranty, a 250 MB quota raised on request — and the two clauses that matter most, on permanent data loss and on what happens when the beta ends.";
const canonical = new URL("/terms/", Astro.site!).toString();
const ogImage = absoluteOg("terms", Astro.site!);

const effective = "12 August 2026";

const eyebrow = "font-size:11px;color:#8aa4d0;margin-bottom:14px;";
const h2 =
  "font-size:clamp(19px,2.2vw,25px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.02em;line-height:1.15;margin-top:56px;";
const h3 =
  "font-size:16px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-top:32px;color:#e6e6e4;";
const body =
  "margin-top:14px;max-width:68ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#8a8a86;";
const cardStyle =
  "border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;padding:22px;background:#0c0c0c;margin-top:22px;";
const warnCard =
  "border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16);border-radius:12px;padding:22px;background:#111;margin-top:22px;";

const forbidden = [
  "Storing or distributing material that is illegal where you are, or under German law",
  "Attacking the service — attempting to overload it, break into other accounts, or bypass the quota and rate limits",
  "Automated bulk registration of accounts",
  "Reselling the hosted service as your own",
];
---

<LandingLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogImage={ogImage}>
  <div
    style="font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#e6e6e4;background:#0a0a0a;min-height:100vh;"
  >
    <GlassNav active="legal" />

    <section id="top" style="padding:128px 28px 70px;">
      <div style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;">
        <div class="mono up" style={eyebrow}>Legal</div>
        <h1
          style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,50px);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;"
        >
          Beta Terms
        </h1>
        <p style={body}>
          Effective {effective}. These terms govern the free Myne beta — the hosted sync service at
          sync.myne.md, the web app at app.example.com, and the desktop and mobile apps that use them.
        </p>

        <div style={cardStyle}>
          <div class="mono up" style={eyebrow}>The short version</div>
          <p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#8a8a86;">
            The beta is free and takes no payment. There is no warranty and no service level —
            software this young breaks. If you lose your password and your recovery phrase, your
            notes are gone permanently, and nobody can recover them. When the beta ends your account
            keeps working; a paid tier, if one ever exists, will be a choice and not a condition.
            And if the service ever shuts down, you get 90 days' notice with export working the
            whole time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 style={h2}>What this is</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          A free, non-commercial test of software still in development. No payment is taken, no
          subscription exists, and nothing on this service is sold to you. That is not a temporary
          promotion — it is the basis on which the service is currently offered, and much of what
          follows rests on it.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          You must be at least 16 years old to use Myne. That is the age at which consent to data
          processing is valid under German law.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Your account</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          An account is a 20-character number, generated on your device. We ask for no email
          address, no name and no payment details — which means we also have no way to identify you
          if you lose access, and no way to verify that someone contacting us is you.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          You are responsible for keeping your password and your recovery phrase. They are the only
          things that open your notes.
        </p>

        <!-- ── The clause the whole architecture makes necessary, and the -->
        <!-- one most competitors' terms omit. It gets its own card.       -->
        <div style={warnCard}>
          <div class="mono up" style={eyebrow}>Permanent data loss</div>
          <p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#e6e6e4;">
            <strong
              >If you lose your password and your recovery phrase, your notes cannot be recovered.
              Not by you, and not by us.</strong
            >
          </p>
          <p style="margin:14px 0 0;max-width:64ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#8a8a86;">
            This is not a support limitation that a determined request could get around. Your keys
            are derived on your device from secrets we never receive; what we hold is ciphertext we
            have no key for. There is no reset link, no security question and no administrative
            override, because building one would mean holding a key — and holding a key would mean
            being able to read your notes, and being compelled to.
          </p>
          <p style="margin:14px 0 0;max-width:64ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#8a8a86;">
            Write your recovery phrase down and keep it somewhere safe. It is the entire backup
            plan.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 style={h2}>No warranty, no service level</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          The service is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. There is no uptime
          commitment, no support commitment and no guarantee that a given feature keeps working the
          way it does today. Data loss caused by a bug is possible; keep your own backups. The app
          can export everything you have, and doing so occasionally is a reasonable habit during a
          beta.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Quota and limits</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          Each account gets 250 MB of encrypted storage. Ask and we will raise it, free — write to
          <a href="mailto:hello@myne.md" style="color:#8aa4d0;">hello@myne.md</a>. There is no limit
          on the number of accounts the service accepts.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          Rate limits apply per account, to keep the service available. They are not billing
          mechanisms and there is nothing to buy your way past.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>What you may not do</h2>
        <ul style={body + "padding-left:20px;"}>
          {forbidden.map((x) => <li style="margin-top:8px;">{x}</li>)}
        </ul>

        <h3 style={h3}>How moderation actually works here</h3>
        <p style={body}>
          <strong style="color:#e6e6e4;"
            >We cannot see your content, so we do not filter it in advance — and we could not if we
            wanted to.</strong
          > There is no scanning, no automated review and no proactive detection of anything, because
          everything stored here is encrypted with keys we do not hold.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          When a substantiated report reaches us, what we can do is act at the account level:
          freeze the account, or delete it. We cannot remove one note and leave the rest, because we
          cannot tell them apart. The reporting procedure is on the
          <a href="/notice/" style="color:#8aa4d0;">notice page</a>.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          We may freeze or delete an account that is being used for something in the list above, or
          where a legal obligation requires it. A freeze blocks writing and leaves reading intact,
          so a frozen account can still be exported.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>When the beta ends</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          <strong style="color:#e6e6e4;">Your account keeps working.</strong> The end of the beta is
          not an expiry date: accounts and their data carry on exactly as they are. If a paid tier appears
          later, it will be an option you can take or leave — not a gate that closes in front of data
          you already have.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          We are stating this because the opposite has happened to people. When a well-known
          encrypted service shut down in 2024, its users found that nothing in its terms had
          promised them anything at all.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>If the service shuts down</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          Should we ever stop running the hosted service, you get
          <strong style="color:#e6e6e4;">at least 90 days' notice</strong>. Throughout that period
          the service stays reachable and export keeps working, so you can take your notes with you.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          After that, you are still not stuck: the server is
          <a href="https://github.com/myne-md" rel="noopener" style="color:#8aa4d0;">open source</a>
          under the AGPL, and the client can point at any server you run. A shutdown on our side ends
          our hosting, not your ability to use Myne.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Donations</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          Donations are welcome and buy nothing. Donors get no badge, no early access, no priority
          support, no additional storage and no influence over what gets built. The service is
          identical for everyone, whether they have donated or not.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          This is deliberate and it is the line that keeps a donation a donation. The moment a
          contribution bought something in return, it would stop being a gift and start being a
          purchase — with everything that follows from that.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Liability</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          We are liable for intent and gross negligence, and for injury to life, body or health,
          under the statutory rules. For ordinary negligence we are liable only for breach of an
          obligation essential to the purpose of this agreement, and then limited to the damage
          typically foreseeable for a service of this kind. Because the service is provided free of
          charge, German law limits liability further; nothing here is intended to extend beyond
          what the law provides.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          Mandatory statutory liability, including under the Produkthaftungsgesetz, is unaffected.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Ending it</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          You can delete your account at any time, from inside the app. It removes your vault,
          attachments, device registry and login verifier; backups follow within 14 days. There is
          nothing to cancel and nothing to pay.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          If these terms change in a way that affects you, the apps show you the new version rather
          than swapping the page quietly. Each version carries its effective date, and the previous
          text stays in the site's public history.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Governing law</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          German law applies, excluding its conflict-of-law rules. If you are a consumer, this does
          not deprive you of the protection of mandatory provisions of the law of your country of
          residence.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@myne.md" style="color:#8aa4d0;">hello@myne.md</a>. How we
          handle data is in the <a href="/privacy/" style="color:#8aa4d0;">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <p style={body + "margin-top:44px;font-size:14px;color:#6f6f6c;"}>
          Deutsche Fassung: <a href="/nutzungsbedingungen/" style="color:#8aa4d0;"
            >Nutzungsbedingungen</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</LandingLayout>
